I used to think my teenage video editing phase was a total waste of time.

Years ago, I spent countless hours editing videos and learning how to sync clips to audio beats. Tbh, my parents probably thought I was just wasting my time in front of a screen instead of studying.

But as a student founder, those random creative skills ended up being a major advantage.

When we were launching STRAYED, we needed high-quality promotional content but had zero budget for a production agency. I decided to write a custom script to automate some of our video transitions and help sync raw streetwear footage to trending audio loops.

One of the promotional reels we edited hit over 80,000 views on Instagram, bringing a huge wave of organic traffic to our site.

It proved to me that no skill you learn is ever truly wasted. The weird creative side projects you do at fifteen often end up powering your startup marketing at twenty.

What random childhood hobby has unexpectedly helped you in your professional work?

#founder #contentcreator #marketing
